			"Message": "style(Grove): Fix import path to use PascalCase module name\n\nUpdate the import statement in Source/main.rs to use `Grove` (PascalCase) instead of `grove` (lowercase), aligning with the project's naming conventions as specified in CLAUDE.md.\n\nThis ensures consistency with the project's PascalCase naming standard for modules and crates.",
			"SHA": "80c11d254d18fa3a42f94b33840df8b33082f818"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:53:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				71,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Grove): Fix string ownership in LanguageNamespace provider registration\n\nThe `provider_type` parameter was being used as a borrowed `&str` reference in multiple places within the `register()` method, causing potential lifetime issues when passed to `store.insert()` and used in `format!()` calls.\n\nNow the method converts `provider_type` to an owned `String` (`ProviderTypeOwned`) first, then passes a reference to that owned string to `store.insert()`. This ensures consistent ownership semantics and eliminates the reference-to-temporary issue.\n\nAlso: simplify import paths in the module header and apply minor formatting consistency across method signatures.",
			"SHA": "fbe35236c67dc54460c427bf80634673e4a3dd6d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T03:40:27Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				71,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Docs): Update Documentation/Rust submodule to latest commit\n\nAdvance the Documentation/Rust submodule from 8b6224b9a21f0173f80289d43da739603bef4b2c to 0c52283d9164226ce64b72373010a20fe454fa6f.\n\nThis brings in the latest documentation updates for the Rust components.",
			"SHA": "9a17b08dd769b45dde169694f8e6e499923e142d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T03:35:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				71,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Grove): Forward provider registrations to Mountain via transport\n\nWire the VSCodeAPI and LanguageNamespace to an optional Transport for forwarding provider registrations to Mountain. When a transport is wired:\n1. VSCodeAPI::new_with_transport() creates a facade connected to Mountain\n2. LanguageNamespace stores the transport and forwards each register_*_provider call via send_no_response as a JSON notification matching Mountain's GenericNotification format\n3. The notification includes handle, language_selector, and extension_id\n\nThis enables Mountain's ProviderRegistry to track registrations from Grove extensions, completing the P4 task from the previous commit. Local ProviderStore still handles disposal cleanup.\n\nAlso: reformat rustflags arrays in .cargo/config.toml for consistency, and expand column widths in DeepDive.md tables for readability.",
			"SHA": "cb994d4a334fda4c874b8555b4a6dfd0aa98d954"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T02:54:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				71,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Properly store Common-library TransportConfig in TransportAdapter\n\nPreviously the config() method returned a temporary config on each call (constructed from GroveTransportConfig fields), or paniced with unimplemented!() for the reference return type. Now the adapter:\n1. Stores a `common_config:TransportConfig` field built at construction time\n2. Adds BuildCommonConfig() method to map GroveTransportConfig fields to CommonLibrary TransportConfig\n3. Returns the stored reference from config() - no allocations on repeated calls\n\nThis eliminates the unimplemented!() panic and removes repeated config construction overhead. The Common config is now built once and cached for the lifetime of the adapter.",
			"SHA": "5b5f89d2ca49f6a9da7a5d8e0f178321b9e50c25"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1779544355827
}